{"game_id":2026020134,"away":"PIT","home":"VGK","split":{"name":"Girard","side":0,"sec":1754},"lede":"Vegas had last change, so Ryan Craig picked most of these matchups. Pittsburgh played without Egor Chinakhov and Hendrix Lapierre and lost Samuel Girard after 9:14 of the second.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"Marner’s line drew Crosby’s line","text":"Ryan Craig sent Howden, W. Karlsson and Marner out for 8:14 of their 12:16 at 5-on-5 against Rakell, Crosby and Rust (67%, about 31% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.28 to 0.22 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Kindel’s line","text":"Connelly, Hertl and Lavoie spent 7:04 of their 13:47 at 5-on-5 against Kuzmenko, Kindel and Robertson (51%, about 25% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.36 to 0.25 expected goals."},{"kind":"swing","head":"One matchup went wrong","text":"Gatcomb, Dowd and Bowman kept drawing Pittsburgh’s second line, Koivunen, Novak and Malkin. In those 5:28 Pittsburgh had 0.72 expected goals to Vegas’s 0.06. Pittsburgh scored one of its two goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Girard left, the lines changed but the matchups held","text":"The matchups stayed: Marner’s line against Pittsburgh’s first line (76% before, 57% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Pittsburgh had 1.12 to 0.98 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Girard left and 1.83 to 0.95 after. Pittsburgh trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Ryan Craig matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 47% of its time against one opposing line, against 40% to 48% in his first five.","periods":{"all":{"0":{"rows":[{"label":"L1","names":["Rakell","Crosby","Rust"],"sec":994,"mixed":9,"vs":[273,494,112,115],"xgf":0.46,"xga":0.65,"gf":0,"ga":1,"cells":[[0.12,0.05,0,0],[0.22,0.28,0,0],[0.0,0.1,0,1],[0.12,0.22,0,0]]},{"label":"L2","names